---
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';
import { labels } from '../data/intelligence';
import { sourceRules, sourceTiers } from '../data/review';
const sections = [['what', 'What intelligence means here'], ['labels', 'Fact, analysis, projection and opinion'], ['sources', 'Sources'], ['data', 'Data and charts'], ['limits', 'What we do not claim'], ['sample', 'Sample data'], ['corrections', 'Corrections']].map(([id, title]) => ({ id, title }));
---
<PolicyPage title="Research Policy" lede="How Native Media collects, checks and presents information in its intelligence and research products." sections={sections}>
  <h2 id="what">What intelligence means here</h2>
  <p>At Native Media, intelligence means collecting, organizing, analyzing and presenting relevant information to support understanding, informed decisions, institutional engagement and strategic communication. It is based on credible, published sources.</p>
  <h2 id="labels">Fact, analysis, projection and opinion</h2>
  <p>We keep these apart and label them:</p>
  <ul>{labels.map(([t, d]) => <li><strong>{t}.</strong> {d}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
  <p>Our institutional publications use a stated source hierarchy:</p>
  <ul>{sourceTiers.map((t) => <li><strong>{t.tier}: {t.title}.</strong> {t.items.join('; ')}.</li>)}</ul>
  <p>Rules we follow:</p>
  <ul>{sourceRules.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2 id="data">Data and charts</h2>
  <p>Every chart and data exhibit shows its title, indicator, reporting period, source, units and any explanatory notes. Charts have a text alternative and a data table. Each edition or report states its data cut-off date.</p>
  <h2 id="limits">What we do not claim</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Native Media does not claim confidential intelligence capabilities, government intelligence affiliations or privileged access.</li>
    <li>We do not promise predictive accuracy or guaranteed decision outcomes.</li>
    <li>We state the limitations of each analysis.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="sample">Sample data</h2>
  <p>Where we build prototypes, any sample data is clearly marked as illustrative and is never presented as fact.</p>
  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>Errors are corrected openly. See the <a href="/editorial-policy#corrections">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>
</PolicyPage>
